            "name": "getAccountsRecPrompt"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773062869206"
          },
          "code": "GETACCOUNTSRECPROMPT",
          "id": "1773062715573",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773062847732_1",
              "name": "agentName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$workflow.$name}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ExtractAccountRecPrompt",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const defaultMainPrompt = \n`-- TASK @ DEFAULT VERSION --\nlet possibleAccounts =resolvedAccountsVar\n\nOperate on possibleAccounts for the rest of the prompt.\n\nYour task is to process a single Accounts resolved entity and return a structured JSON object for that entity only.\nYou must never output explanations or commentary—only the final JSON.\n\nThis topic receives exactly one object E where E.name == \"Accounts\".\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINSTRUCTIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Read the input Accounts entity object E.\n\n2. Always process E even if resolvedValues or matches are empty.\n\n3. This topic does NOT fetch defaults, MRU, MFU, or compute scores.\n   All candidate generation and enrichment is already done upstream.\n   This topic ONLY:\n     - orders matches\n     - limits output\n     - normalizes structure\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTERMINAL CASES (DO NOT CHANGE)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n4. If E.resolvedValues.length == 1 AND\n   E.resolvedValues[0].status == \"ORA_EXACT_MATCH\" AND\n   E.resolvedValues[0].matches.length == 1:\n\n    - Ensure predictionRank = \"1\"\n    - Ensure companyId, companyName, costCenterId, costCenterName are grouped under fieldValue\n    - Return E unchanged otherwise.\n\n5. If E.resolvedValues.length == 1 AND\n   E.resolvedValues[0].status is \"ORA_NOT_RESOLVED\" OR \"ORA_NO_ACCESS\":\n\n    - Return E unchanged.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nORDERING LOGIC\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n6. Collect ALL matches from ALL resolvedValues into one list\n   preserving original encounter order.\n\n   Ignore inputValues completely for output purposes.\n\n6a. Similarity evaluation (MANDATORY):\n    - For each resolvedValue:\n        * Join inputValues into a single string S (if present)\n    - For each match:\n        * Build matchText using companyName + costCenterName (if present)\n    - Compute semantic similarity between S and matchText\n      based on meaning, not exact string match\n    - For each match, keep the highest similarity score\n      across all resolvedValues\n\n6b. Order candidateMatches by similarity score descending.\n    If scores tie, preserve original encounter order.\n\n7. Separate matches into:\n    a. invalidMatch:\n       predictionTypeCode == \"ORA_RESOLVED_INVALID\" (at most one)\n\n    b. candidateMatches:\n       predictionTypeCode NOT IN\n       (\"ORA_RESOLVED_INVALID\", \"ORA_NOT_RESOLVED\", \"ORA_NO_ACCESS\")\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT BUILDING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n8. If invalidMatch exists:\n    - status must be \"ORA_RECOMMENDATION\"\n    - Output matches in this exact order:\n        1. invalidMatch\n        2. First 3 candidateMatches (if available)\n    - Assign predictionRank = \"1\", \"2\", \"3\" to candidateMatches only\n    - invalidMatch must NOT have predictionRank\n\n9. If invalidMatch does NOT exist:\n    - status must be \"ORA_RECOMMENDATION\"\n    - Output first 3 candidateMatches preserving similarity order\n    - Assign predictionRank = \"1\", \"2\", \"3\"\n\n10. For all candidateMatches in output:\n     - predictionDisplayRule = \"ORA_REQUEST_USER_INPUT\"\n     - predictionSource = \"ORA_COMPLETION_ASSISTANT\"\n     - ruleCode = \"\"\n     - fieldName = \"Accounts\" if present\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nFINAL STRUCTURE (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n11. Replace resolvedValues with exactly ONE item:\n    {\n      matches: <final matches>,\n      status: \"ORA_RECOMMENDATION\"\n    }\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nFINAL OUTPUT (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou must return a JSON object with EXACTLY these two fields:\n\n{\n  \"accountsRec\": <the reordered Accounts entity E>,\n  \"reasoning\": \"<one short sentence explaining what was done>\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- accountsRec must contain the Accounts entity in the same structure as input E,\n  with resolvedValues replaced by the final ordered/limited matches.\n- reasoning must be a short string (max 1 sentence).\n- Do not include any other fields.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTRICT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Maximum 4 matches in output when ORA_RESOLVED_INVALID exists; otherwise maximum 3.\n- ORA_RESOLVED_INVALID, if present, must always be first.\n- ORA_RESOLVED_INVALID must never have predictionRank.\n- Do not fabricate matches.\n- Do not change predictionTypeCode.\n- Do not introduce ORA_RESOLVED_INVALID if not present.\n- Do not preserve inputValues in output.\n- Return exactly one Accounts entity inside accountsRec.\n- Only output valid JSON.`;\n\n\nconst out = $context.$nodes.GETACCOUNTSRECPROMPT.$output ;\nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nlet mainPrompt = prompts?.find(p => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultMainPrompt;\n\nlet prompt = {\n  mainPrompt: mainPrompt,\n};\nreturn prompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769447321965"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACTACCOUNTRECPROMPT",
          "id": "1773062869206",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        }
